WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
John: Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.739
It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer
real questions from real Nerdfighters.

00:00:03.739 --> 00:00:05.130
Let's get - Uh oh.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.490
It's a wild Hank, and he's goatobombing me.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:12.179
Hank: Yesterday, we were out to dinner, and
I made a dumb face in a photograph and everybody

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:13.510
at the table decided it was goatobombing.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.280
John: Yeah, because it was photobombing but
he looked like a goat.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.280
Hank: Hnng.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.810
John: Speaking of goats, our first question
is, would you rather fight one John-sized

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:23.880
goat or three goat-sized Johns?

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.080
Hank: I'd rather fight one John-sized goat.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.570
You are crafty; making you a goat would make
you easier to fight.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.029
There are definitely goats bigger than you.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:33.321
John: Ah, I don't think so.

00:00:33.321 --> 00:00:35.660
I think I might be bigger than any goat by
weight.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.120
Hank: Siri, are there goats bigger than my
brother?

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.829
(Siri beep) I'm not sure I understand.

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:43.989
John: I don't understand either; let's go
to the next question.

00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:46.079
Hank: What are your thoughts on goats in sweaters?

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:50.050
John: Oh, you mean like where you have a sweater
and there's a goat on it?

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.220
Hank: No, goats in sweaters.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.329
A sweater wearing a goat.

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:53.329
I mean a goat wearing a sweater.

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:55.820
John: A sweater wearing a goat is a fantastic
idea!

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.700
Did you know goats have rectangular pupils,
by the way?

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.700
Hank: I did know that.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:00:59.700
John: Yeah.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.700
Do you know why?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.720
Hank: They're like horizontal rectangles,
which probably means that they're trying to

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:03.720
look out in more, multiple, like better, better...

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:04.960
John: Peripheral vision.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.330
Hank: I want to know what that's like.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:10.140
I bet the Oculus Rift could like, could, show
me what's it like to be a goat.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.350
Do you wanna get another question?

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.350
John: Yes.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.400
Hank: Let's do another question.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.950
How many llamas is one goat worth?

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.460
John: Can I just pause real quick, Hank, and
ask why all the questions are about goats?

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.720
Hank: The thing is, I just asked for questions,
and there just happened to be a bunch about

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:23.720
goats.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.720
And I also asked them to ask questions about
goats?

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:25.720
John: Oh!

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:26.720
I see your tweet.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.410
"Goat questions preferred."

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.159
Who can do the best impression of a goat.

00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:32.350
Hank: You want to go first?

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.350
John: No.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.350
I want to go not at all.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.290
I'm happy to lose if Hank will try.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:37.670
Hank: (Attempts goat noise)

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.310
John: That was so bad.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:40.450
Hank: (Makes goat noise again)

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.450
John: (Laughs)

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.450
Hank: That's what they sound like.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.130
You've never even met a goat.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.130
You don't know what they sound like.

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.130
That was perfect.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.369
John: That's not true!

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:48.369
That's not true.

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:52.810
Hank, I made the Internet's number one video
about goat mating.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.920
Don't tell me I've never seen a goat.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.350
I've seen a goat do it.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.320
Hank: And they make that noise.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.420
John: Nope!

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.522
Hank: (Attempts goat noise)

00:02:00.522 --> 00:02:02.720
John: This is a question that I don't think
you'll find particularly difficult, Hank.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.810
Would you rather have a goat eat your ear
or would you rather eat a goat's ear?

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.319
Hank: How is that even a question?

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:09.319
(Laughs)

00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:13.420
John: It's like the old question "Would you
rather eat five pine cones or poop one?"

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:19.110
Like as unpleasant as it would be to eat five
pine cones, obviously that's the better option.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.100
Hank: I would rather eat a goat's ear than
any other part of a goat.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.340
Because you could take the goat's ear and
it would be fine!

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.790
John: Not fine, how would you feel if you
were earless?

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:31.810
I noticed that you and I have different iPhone
passwords, so if you want to ask another question

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.860
you're gonna have to log in.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.030
Hank: John, where does the word "goat" come
from?

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.240
John: Oh I know that actually.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.390
It comes from Old English.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.010
What is your favorite breed of goat?

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.010
Hank: Brand?

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.010
Brand of goat?

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.010
John: Breed!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.320
Hank: I'm gonna go with the American mountain
goat.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.730
John: I was gonna say The Mountain Goats too.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.200
Hank: Which kind of mountain goat though?

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.620
John: Oh, John Darnielle probably.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.510
If you had seven goats between you, what would
you name them?

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.490
I would like to have four of the goats.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:55.490
That's all that matters to me.

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:58.850
(Hank laughs) I would like to make sure that
if we have seven goats between us, I have

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.080
the four and you have the three.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.959
Hank: How about, alternatively, you have all
seven?

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:04.959
John: Wait, I've rethought my answer.

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:06.569
I would like to give you the seven goats.

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:08.410
(Hank laughs) Alright I took another guess
at your iPhone password.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:09.680
I still didn't get it.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.720
Hank: Goaticorn or unigoat?

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.269
John: Yeah so we're talking about two different
animals.

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:18.610
The goaticorn is a goat with a unicorn horn,
the unigoat is a unicorn with a goat head.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:20.300
Or as I like to call it, a horse.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.180
(Hank laughs) And I'm gonna go with the unigoat.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:28.180
Here is a non-goat question for you Hank,
what really gets your goat?

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:34.420
(Both laugh)

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.739
Hank: When awful people succeed.

00:03:38.739 --> 00:03:40.902
John: Hank, thank you so much for doing question
Tuesday with me.

00:03:40.902 --> 00:03:43.660
Hank: Happy birthday, it was your birthday
yesterday, everybody say happy birthday to

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:44.660
that guy.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.750
John: Ah, I will see you on Friday.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.750
And now.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.049
Hank: Okay we have to go cause we're out of
tape so blaaah!

